d-trailing","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"name":"scan","size":14,"tone":"muted","visible":false},"id":"r-dismissed-glyph","type":"Icon"},{"config":{"flex":"0 0 auto","text":{"$i18n":"comments.sample.time.w2"},"tone":"muted","variant":"label"},"id":"r-dismissed-time","type":"Text"},{"config":{"align":"center","direction":"horizontal","flex":"0 0 auto","gap":2},"id":"r-dismissed-count","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"name":"message-circle","size":12,"tone":"muted"},"id":"r-dismissed-count-icon","type":"Icon"},{"config":{"text":"2","tone":"muted","variant":"label"},"id":"r-dismissed-count-n","type":"Text"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Stack"},{"config":{"description":{"$i18n":"empty.body"},"icon":"message-circle","title":{"$i18n":"empty.title"},"visible":false},"id":"e-none","slots":{"actions":[{"config":{"icon":"message-circle-plus","label":{"$i18n":"comments.startCommenting"},"size":"sm","variant":"outline"},"id":"e-none-start","type":"Button"}]},"type":"EmptyState"},{"config":{"icon":"message-circle","title":{"$i18n":"comments.noneInFilter"},"visible":false},"id":"e-filter","type":"EmptyState"},{"config":{"align":"start","direction":"vertical","gap":8,"padding":"24px 16px","visible":false},"id":"e-resolved","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"name":"circle-check","size":20,"tone":"success"},"id":"e-resolved-icon","type":"Icon"},{"config":{"text":{"$i18n":"allCaughtUp"},"tone":"highlighted","value":3,"variant":"ui","weight":"medium"},"id":"e-resolved-text","type":"Text"},{"config":{"label":{"$i18n":"comments.showResolved"},"size":"sm","variant":"outline"},"id":"e-resolved-show","type":"Button"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Stack"},{"config":{"align":"center","borderTop":true,"direction":"horizontal","gap":6,"padding":"8px 12px","visible":false},"id":"workspace-footer","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"name":"globe","size":14,"tone":"muted"},"id":"workspace-footer-icon","type":"Icon"},{"config":{"label":{"$i18n":"comments.workspaceFooter.one"},"size":"sm","value":1,"variant":"link-muted"},"id":"workspace-footer-link","type":"Button"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"RootShell"},"name":"Comments tab","spec":{"accessibility":["The filter group is named \"Show comments\" and each button announces whether it is pressed; each group is a list named by its heading, and the thread list is a region named \"Comments on this View\".","A row is one button that names the thread, its author, its target and its time; status is a glyph with its label, never color alone."],"constraints":["Built only from Adapter Widgets (Stack, Text, Button, Icon, Avatar, SegmentedControl, Segment, EmptyState, Alert); no Widget outside the Adapter catalog.","The strings of the app are copied under the same Locale keys; a count binds through value (the heading, the filter buttons, the footer), and the filter button label and the group headings that the app composes from a label and a number are written as one key per group, comments.group.*Count and comments.filterCount.*.","Each group is shown or hidden by a Variant; the list is not scrolled and its rows do not highlight on hover. The glyph column of a row (why its pin is not on the canvas) is hidden here and shown in Comments tab: rows.","The Comment on View button is absent on a phone in the app (phones never start comments, Rule 01a116f0-90e2-7a5a-b9d8-c80984d034ea); a Widget cannot depend on the viewport here, so it stays in every context. The tab strip is the one of Right panel: tabs and Flows.","Every visible string is bound with $i18n except identities (author names, Widget types and ids, Variant names); en-US and zh-TW keep identical key sets.","Visual language follows the Quiet Canvas design system in DESIGN.md."],"decisions":[],"entryConditions":["A member opened a View page and the Comments tab of its right panel, which is the first tab and the one the page opens on; the tab shows the number of unresolved threads on this View.","The base state lists the threads on the View as a whole, then those ready for review, then the open ones; the filter shows Open and Ready for review, and Resolved is off.","The render context selects one Workspace viewport preset, one Locale and one theme; the tab is Workbench chrome, so its text follows the Workbench language and is baked here per Locale. The thread titles, names and times are sample content from the Checkout View of this Workspace."],"intent":"Show the Comments tab of a View's right panel as built from Adapter Widgets only: the list companion to the canvas pins, filtered by status, grouped by what a person can do with each thread, with the one-click Comment on View entry and the way to the Workspace comments that never sit on a canvas.","interactionRules":["The three filter buttons show or hide threads by status and each carries its count; a pressed one is filled. Resolved off keeps resolved and dismissed threads out of the list, and with every thread resolved the tab says everything is caught up and offers Show resolved.","Threads group as View (comments on the whole View, led by the RootShell anchor), Ready for review, Open, Not shown on canvas, Can't be placed, Other Variants, then Resolved and Dismissed when the filter shows them. A group heading carries its count and, for four of them, an icon.","A thread whose Widget no longer exists, or whose every named Variant is gone, is kept in Can't be placed with the reason in words and Re-anchor; a thread scoped to another Variant is listed under Other Variants with a Switch to button; a thread whose Widget gets no geometry stream is listed under Not shown on canvas, with the pin-filter hint.","Comment on View starts a comment on the RootShell without picking a Widget; Start commenting (shown when there are no threads) enters comment mode. Workspace comments never appear in the list: a footer link says how many there are and opens them in Reviews.","A row opens its thread and reveals its pin; J and K move between rows."],"references":[{"label":"Phase 5 of the closed loop: dogfood coverage of the core surfaces","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/379#discussioncomment-19257377"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"view","viewId":"b1c7e306-4a1d-4c2e-9f31-7a4c0d2e6b06"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"view","viewId":"7f3d7780-3cb9-4e57-8f0b-2e8d569905c1"}],"requirements":["01a11544-5170-7aec-8d4b-56b8faacfca2","01a194f5-77d9-73a4-bfc3-29e627e15cd6","01a194f5-79d0-7b35-8896-5c5a959adf86","01a194f5-7bca-78b8-933d-bcd2184fd118"]},"variants":{"all-caught-up":{"state":{"e-filter":{"visible":false},"e-none":{"visible":false},"e-resolved":{"visible":true},"filter-open":{"variant":"secondary"},"filter-ready":{"variant":"secondary"},"filter-resolved":{"variant":"ghost"},"g-dismissed":{"visible":false},"g-open":{"visible":false},"g-other":{"visible":false},"g-overcap":{"visible":false},"g-ready":{"visible":false},"g-resolved":{"visible":false},"g-unplaced":{"visible":false},"g-view":{"visible":false}}},"all-groups":{"requirements":["01a11544-5170-7aec-8d4b-56b8faacfca2","01a11544-5dad-7d4c-b8e4-e1080c880bda","01a11544-5d87-7784-8b47-59de8187e492","01a11658-2611-7395-92f0-372dd841ed6a","01a11544-524d-7fd7-aa5e-d3f4388bdd41"],"state":{"e-filter":{"visible":false},"e-none":{"visible":false},"e-resolved":{"visible":false},"filter-open":{"variant":"secondary"},"filter-ready":{"variant":"secondary"},"filter-resolved":{"variant":"secondary"},"g-dismissed":{"visible":true},"g-open":{"visible":true},"g-other":{"visible":true},"g-overcap":{"visible":true},"g-ready":{"visible":true},"g-resolved":{"visible":true},"g-unplaced":{"visible":true},"g-view":{"visible":true},"workspace-footer":{"visible":true}}},"cannot-be-placed":{"requirements":["01a11544-5228-70b4-96be-e5e032bb3b63","01a11544-524d-7fd7-aa5e-d3f4388bdd41","01a11544-5d60-705e-b88a-d2e8743cba14"],"state":{"e-filter":{"visible":false},"e-none":{"visible":false},"e-resolved":{"visible":false}